Florence is an extensible scalable virtual keyboard for X11. You need it if
you cannot use a real keyboard (for example because of a handicap, a broken
keyboard, or a tablet PC) but can use a pointing device.

This port tracks the FrauBSD continuation of Florence after the SourceForge
project stalled at 0.6.3 (2014). It includes sticky modifiers, a safer Resize
scale path (stock magnifier +/− could crash), Framework-style Fn row layout,
session placement, and a unified greeter mode.
